  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nCurrent upper level pattern shows a low off the northwest Pacific\ncoast with sharp ridging over eastern MT. This is bringing high \nclouds across central MT with lifting fog and low stratus across \nfar eastern MT. This pattern is also creating a tight surface \ngradient across southeast MT bringing gusts 30-45 mph through late\nthis evening. Breezy conditions 25-35 mph are expected to \ncontinue into Saturday for this area. Patchy fog is expected again\nacross southeast MT into Saturday morning as well. Saturday into \nSunday, a weak surface pressure gradient is expected to form \nacross the Paradise Valley, bringing breezy conditions with gusts\n30-40 mph and about a 25% chance for gusts to at least 50 mph at \nLivingston and Nye Sunday morning. Into next week, a more \nsouthwesterly flow builds in a the troughing from the northwest \napproaches. With this, increasing chances of precipitation will \nbegin Tuesday through the remainder of the period. Cooler weather \nis expected to move in mid week with temperatures dropping into \nthe upper 30s to mid 40s. There is still some uncertainty with \nthe exact track of this system which will affect if the region \nsees beneficial precipitation or not. Currently, there is about a \n50-80% chance for at least a quarter inch of precipitation across \nsouth central MT, with about a 25-40% chance for southeast MT and \nnorthern WY. TS",
